  "notes": [
    "These are the numbers of a SYNTHETIC remote-desktop model, not of a real session: a source screen, a bitrate ladder, a rate-limited link with loss and jitter, a bounded transmit queue, a decoder and a display. The run is deterministic (seeded RNG), so the artifact is a regression baseline.",
    "The response curve -- ladder level, delivered fps, cumulative freeze count and latency percentiles vs. time -- is the measurement the plan asks for (J4). A throughput number is not reported: throughput does not describe the feel.",
    "The input-to-photon numbers (J6) pair the operator's input event with the first source frame captured after the event reaches the remote machine, and measure the event to that frame's display time.",
    "The stage costs (encode 4 ms, decode 4 ms, present 1 ms) are the hardware-path figures from the plan's \u00a7B.6 budget table.",
    "The impairment levels are the same family as the transport-floor tiers of tools/benchmark_weaknet.py; the two artifacts can be read side by side."
